 "private/get_transaction_log": {
  "scope": "private",
  "tags": [
   "Account Management",
   "Private"
  ],
  "summary": "Retrieves a detailed transaction log for the authenticated account.",
  "description": "Retrieves a detailed transaction log for the authenticated account. The log includes all account activities such as trades, deposits, withdrawals, transfers, fees, and other balance-affecting operations. Results can be filtered by currency, time range, and `query` keywords. `start_timestamp` must not exceed `end_timestamp`; both values are clamped to the current time, so a future `end_timestamp` is treated as now. The matching window includes `end_timestamp`. `count` defaults to 100 and is capped at 1000. Pass `continuation` (a log id from the previous response) to fetch the next older page. `continuation` is `null` when there are no more entries. To retrieve transactions for a specific subaccount, pass `subaccount_id` from the main account. Removed subaccounts are accepted. The authenticated user id is always applied as a filter. Trade entries executed in Starbase include `starbase_match_id`, `starbase_order_id`, and `starbase_timestamp`. Those fields are omitted on spot trades. Block RFQ allocations appear as `type` `trade allocation` rather than `trade`. When an option expires out of the money, the transaction log type is `expiry`. As there is nothing to settle into futures in this case, this remains the only entry in the transaction log for that expiration. In-the-money expiries use `assignment` or `exercise`, and may be followed by a `future creation` entry. LSP and ADL position moves are logged as `type` `LSP transfer` / `ADL transfer`. Both the liquidated/deleveraged account and the receiving account get that same `type`. A separate optional `role` field (`source` or `destination`) is present on those transfer entries — and also on `liquidation transfer` and `position move` — and is omitted on all other types, including `LSP commission` / `ADL commission` and ordinary `trade`s. Do not confuse `role` with `user_role` (`maker` / `taker`) on trades. Correction entries may include a `related` array of the original log entries they correct. While the platform is starting, the method may return `temporarily_unavailable`. **History Limit:** This API method has **no time limit** - users can query transaction history back to account creation. Note that the CSV export feature available on the website is year-limited to 2023. **Note - This method has distinct API rate limiting requirements:** Sustained rate: 1 request/second. For more information, see [Rate Limits](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/rate-limits). **📖 Related Support Article:** [Transaction log](https://support.deribit.com/hc/en-us/articles/25944587269021-Transaction-log) **📖 Related Article:** [Liquidity Support Program (LSP) API Guide](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/lsp-api-guide) **Scope:** `account:read` [Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_transaction_log)",
  "deprecated": false,
  "params": {
   "currency": {
    "type": "string",
    "enum": [
     "BTC",
     "ETH",
     "STETH",
     "ETHW",
     "USDC",
     "USDT",
     "EURR",
     "SOL",
     "XRP",
     "USYC",
     "PAXG",
     "BNB",
     "USDE"
    ],
    "description": "The currency symbol. **📖 Related Article:** [Using the currency Parameter](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/currency-parameter)"
   },
   "start_timestamp": {
    "type": "integer",
    "description": "The earliest timestamp to return result from (milliseconds since the UNIX epoch)"
   },
   "end_timestamp": {
    "type": "integer",
    "description": "The most recent timestamp to return result from (milliseconds since the UNIX epoch)"
   },
   "query": {
    "type": "string",
    "description": "Space-separated keywords used to filter results. An entry must match every keyword. Keywords are case-sensitive. Transaction types: - ``trade`` - trades - ``deposit`` - deposits - ``withdrawal`` - withdrawals - ``transfer`` - transfers between accounts - ``reward`` - reward transfers - ``mm_lsp_payment`` - market-maker LSP payout transfers - ``settlement`` - funding / session settlement (display type `settlement`) - ``delivery`` - instrument delivery (display type `delivery`) - ``expiry`` - options that expired out of the money - ``assignment`` - assigned options - ``exercise`` - exercised options - ``swap`` - currency swaps - ``correction`` - balance corrections - ``block_trade`` - block trades - ``combo_trade`` - combo trades - ``liquidation`` - liquidation trades and liquidation transfers (display type `liquidation transfer`) - ``lsp`` - LSP position moves and commissions (display types `LSP transfer` / `LSP commission`) - ``adl`` - ADL position moves and commissions (display types `ADL transfer` / `ADL commission`) - ``commission`` - LSP/ADL commissions; typically combined with ``lsp`` or ``adl`` - ``position`` - position moves (display type `position move`); also matches `position move transfer` - ``insurance`` - insurance-related transfers - ``insurance_transfer`` - insurance transfers - ``affiliate`` - affiliate payouts - ``partner`` - partner / application fee payouts - ``fee_deposit`` - fee balance deposits - ``fee_balance_transfer`` - fee balance transfers - ``stake_reward`` - staking rewards - ``lock_deposit_balance`` - locked deposit balance - ``unlock_deposit_balance`` - unlocked deposit balance - ``summary`` - settlement summaries - ``options_settlement_summary`` - options settlement summaries - ``negative_balance_fee`` - negative balance fees - ``creation`` - future creation from expired options (display type `future creation`) - ``margin_loan`` - margin loan interest, issuance, and repayment - ``corporate_action_adjustment`` - stock split, rights offering, and spin-off adjustments - ``stock_split`` - stock splits - ``rights_offering`` - rights offerings - ``spin_off`` - spin-offs - ``m_and_a`` - mergers and acquisitions (display type `m&a`) - ``rename`` - instrument renames - ``custody_settlement_fee`` - custody settlement fees - ``sweep_isolated_position`` - isolated position sweeps - ``structured_product_spread`` - structured product spread - ``usdc_reward`` - USDC rewards - ``usdc_reward_received`` - USDC rewards received - ``usdc_platform_reward`` - USDC platform rewards - ``usdc_reward_payment`` - USDC reward payments - ``ethena_reward`` - Ethena rewards - ``buidl_reward`` - BUIDL rewards - ``socialize_loses`` - socialized losses/refunds (display types `socialized fund` / `socialized refund`) Additional filters: - ``maker`` / ``taker`` - trade role - ``open`` / ``close`` - trade kind (`close` also matches deliveries and liquidations) - ``buy`` / ``sell`` - direction - ``option`` / ``future`` / ``spot`` - instrument kind - ``voice_broker`` - voice-broker trades Additional indexed values, depending on type: - deposits — destination address (custody deposits also index custody name and request id) - withdrawals — withdrawal `code` or custody request id (not the destination address) - transfers — counterparty username"
   },
   "count": {
    "type": "integer",
    "description": "Count of transaction log entries returned, default - `100`, maximum - `1000`"
   },
   "subaccount_id": {
    "type": "integer",
    "description": "Id of a subaccount"
   },
   "continuation": {
    "type": "integer",
    "description": "Continuation token for pagination"
   }
  },
  "required": [
   "currency",
   "start_timestamp",
   "end_timestamp"
  ]
 },
